The shopkeeper nods.
He gives me a bigger shirt.
He says, "Madam, please put this on."
I take the shirt.
I go to the shop's small fitting room.
There I put on the bigger shirt.
I look in the mirror.
This is much better compared to the previous shirt.
This shirt is bigger than that one.
I come out of the fitting room happily.
I tell the shopkeeper, "Brother, this size is right."
He takes the small shirt.
He smiles and gives me the receipt.
The exchange is very easy.
So I say thank you to him.
I go home satisfied.
Now my preparation for the monsoon is complete.
